## Fundamental Authoring Practice — TDD (Red → Green)

<!-- PROCESS — keep as-is; this is the harness's non-negotiable law, not a per-project choice. -->
This is the **primary, non-negotiable authoring practice** for every feature and bugfix. It is not one option among many. The full reference is at [.claude/skills/tdd/SKILL.md](./.claude/skills/tdd/SKILL.md) (from the harness-plugin) — these are the standing rules applied on every change.

**No test, no code.** No feature or bugfix is implemented without a failing test authored first at a confirmed seam. This law has no exceptions and overrides all other practices in this file.

### The Loop

1. **Red** — write a failing test first. No test, no code.
2. **Green** — write only enough code to pass the test. No anticipating future tests, no speculative features.
3. **Repeat** — one seam, one test, one minimal implementation per cycle.

### Seams — Confirm Before Writing

A **seam** is the public boundary you test at. Before writing any test, identify which seams are under test and confirm them with the user.

